e parts \"stand as printed\". These amendments were put after Victorian Senator [Bridget McKenzie](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/bridget_mckenzie) (Nationals) proposed that those parts be opposed. These parts related to: * import requirements for assisted repeating action and straight pull repeating action firearms; * removal of open-ended permits for firearms imports; and * merits review of adverse criminal intelligence assessments about firearms licence. ### Amendment text SHEET 3595 > *(1) Schedule 2, Division 1, page 62 (line 2) to page 64 (line 22), to be opposed.* SHEET 3597 > *(2) Schedule 2, Part 6, page 78 (line 1) to page 79 (line 21), to be opposed.* SHEET 3602 > *(2) Schedule 2, item 24, page 24 (lines 21 to 32), subsections 54E(3) and (4) to be opposed.* > > *(5) Schedule 2, item 24, page 28 (lines 17 to 28), subsections 54J(4) and (5) to be opposed.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9814","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-01-20/3"}
